# Cubit UI consistency (locked)

Source of truth: `src/styles/app-shell.css`, `src/brand.ts`, `.cursor/skills/design-guardrails/CUIB.md`. Not `src/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`.

## Do

- Use shell tokens only: `--ink`, `--ink-soft`, `--ink-faint`, `--bg`, `--surface`, `--border`, `--fill`, `--accent` / `--brand` (`#e8650a` light / `#ff7a1a` dark).
- Reuse shell + `src/components/ui/*` (button, input, sheet, dialog). No parallel kits.
- User-facing product name is **Cubit**.
- Divider expand/collapse controls use `.cuib-edge-toggle` with `--horizontal` or `--vertical`. Chevron only — **no circle border**. Keep a 44px transparent hit target and a tight `--bg` knockout so the divider does not show through the glyph. Lucide chevron `size={14}` `strokeWidth={2.2}`.
- Landing stays on landing tokens; do not mix landing colors into `.cuib-app` or shell tokens into marketing without an explicit ask.
- Phone: 768px (`md`); hit targets ~44px; no hover-only menus.

## Do not

- Circled chevron toggles on dividers (sidebar or dashboard), or a divider line showing through the chevron.
- Second palette, cream/terracotta, purple gradients, neon glow, extra display fonts.
- Neon green (`#22c55e`) progress checklists or loading steps — use shell `--accent` / Cubit orange instead.
- Stacked AI-style step cards on quiz/course load screens — one percentage, one status line, hairline progress.
- Restyle the whole shell to ship a small feature.
- Drive-by `build/` artifacts, theme mocks, or unrelated files in UI commits.
- New localStorage/UI preference helpers without a small `*.test.ts` next to them.

Before push / PR: run `.cursor/skills/design-guardrails` and fail closed on blocks.
